            M("Leo", "Not too badly, thanks. When we last spoke, you said my topic was far too wide, so I've narrowed it down. I thought about plastic packaging, but so many people have done that already. So in the end I've focused on electronic waste, especially old mobile phones."),
            F("Dr Price", "Good choice. There's a lot of interesting material on that. I've had a look at the first draft of your slides. The introduction worries me a bit, though."),
            M("Leo", "Is it too technical? I did wonder about all the names of the metals."),
            F("Dr Price", "No, the level is fine for this audience. The problem is that it goes on for too long. You spend nearly three minutes on the history of the mobile phone before you even mention recycling. People will lose interest."),
            M("Leo", "OK, I'll cut that right down."),
            F("Dr Price", "So, what did you find most interesting in your research?"),
            M("Leo", "I already knew that phones contain small amounts of gold and silver. What really surprised me was how many old phones are never recycled at all. Most of them just sit in drawers at home, because people think they might need them one day, or they're worried about their personal data."),
            F("Dr Price", "That's a good point to build on. Now, your slides. The charts are clear, and you don't need any more of them. But there's far too much text. Some slides have whole paragraphs on them. The audience will read the slides instead of listening to you."),
            M("Leo", "So fewer words, and I just say the rest?"),
            F("Dr Price", "Exactly. Keep a few key words on each slide. Have you thought about how to involve the audience?"),
            M("Leo", "I was going to finish with a short quiz."),
            F("Dr Price", "That can work, but at the end people are usually tired, and it takes longer than you think. What about something quicker near the beginning?"),
