        return new(2,
            "You will hear a park ranger welcoming a group of visitors to a country park.",
            [
                M("Ranger", "Good morning, everyone, and welcome to Pine Valley Country Park. I'm Tom, one of the rangers here. Before you head off, I'd like to tell you a little about the park and explain where everything is."),
                M("Ranger", "A lot of visitors assume that this land was always farmland, because of the old stone walls you can see around the fields. But for over a hundred years, this whole valley was actually a stone quarry. When the quarry closed in the 1960s, the deep pit slowly filled with rainwater, and that's how the lake was formed. The park was opened to the public twenty years later."),
                M("Ranger", "Dogs are very welcome here, and for most of the year they can run freely. However, from March to July, which is the nesting season, dogs must be kept on a lead anywhere near the lake, because many birds nest on the ground along the shore."),
                M("Ranger", "Our guided nature walk is on today as usual. It still leaves from right here outside the visitor centre, and it lasts about two hours, as it always does. The only difference is that it starts at eleven today instead of ten, because our guide is running a little late."),
                M("Ranger", "One very important safety point. You may see people in wetsuits on the lake. They're members of the rowing club, and they have special training. Swimming in the lake is not permitted anywhere, at any time. The water is very deep, because of the old quarry, and it's extremely cold even in summer."),
                M("Ranger", "Now, let me explain where things are. You should all have a copy of the map. We're at the visitor centre, in the middle of the southern edge of the park, so if you look straight ahead, you're facing north, towards the lake."),
                M("Ranger", "If you have children with you, the first place they'll want to go is the adventure playground. Take the path that goes up towards the lake, but bear left. Before you reach the lake, you'll see the playground on your left, just between us and the lake."),
                M("Ranger", "Bird watchers should head for the bird hide. Go round the western side of the lake, and keep going beyond the top of it. The hide is right on the western edge of the park, among the reeds, just north of the lake."),
                M("Ranger", "For those of you staying overnight, the campsite is as far from the road as possible, in the north-eastern corner of the park. It's a quiet spot, surrounded by trees."),
                M("Ranger", "If you'd like to have lunch outdoors, the picnic area is on the eastern side of the park. From the car park, follow the path straight north along the eastern fence, and you'll come to the picnic tables right beside the fence, level with the middle of the lake."),
                M("Ranger", "The forest trail is our longest walk, at about eight kilometres. It starts at a wooden gate on the northern edge of the park. Walk up the western side of the lake, and the gate is straight ahead of you at the far end, slightly to the left of the lake, not in the corner."),
                M("Ranger", "And finally, if you'd prefer to explore on two wheels, you can hire a bike from the cycle hire hut. It's on the same side of the park as the visitor centre, right down in the south-western corner. It's open until five o'clock."),
                M("Ranger", "The ranger station, where we keep the first aid equipment, is just to the east of the lake, if you need us. Have a wonderful day."),
            ],
            [
                new("mcq", Abc, null,
                [
                    Mcq(11, "What was the park before it opened to the public?", ["farmland", "a quarry", "a forest"], "B",
