        "You will hear two students, Nadia and Josh, discussing their research on students who have part-time jobs.",
        [
            M("Josh", "Right, Nadia, we've got all the questionnaires back, so I think we should go through the main findings before we start writing."),
            F("Nadia", "Good idea. So, first of all, the number of students who work. It was about sixty per cent overall, which is roughly what the national surveys say, so no surprise there."),
            M("Josh", "No. But I was surprised by which students were working. I'd assumed that final-year students would work most, because they've built up more debt."),
            F("Nadia", "Me too. But it was actually the first-years. More than two thirds of them had a job, compared with under half of the final-years. Maybe final-years are too busy with their dissertations."),
            M("Josh", "Possibly. And what sort of work were they doing? I expected shop work to come top."),
            F("Nadia", "Retail was second, but restaurants and cafés were well ahead. Tutoring paid the best, but only a handful of people were doing it."),
            M("Josh", "OK. Now, there was a problem with the question about hours, wasn't there? We had to take out about fifteen responses."),
            F("Nadia", "Yes, because some people clearly gave the number of hours they worked in a month, not in a week, even though the question said weekly. Someone said they worked eighty hours a week!"),
            M("Josh", "We should mention that in the limitations section. So, what about the link between working and grades? That's the key question really."),
            F("Nadia", "Well, for students working up to about fifteen hours a week, there wasn't any real difference in their marks. But above fifteen hours, marks were clearly lower. So I think we can say there's a clear link, but only above a certain number of hours."),
            M("Josh", "Agreed. And the benefits? I was sure most people would say it looked good on their CV."),
            F("Nadia", "So was I. And obviously many of them mentioned the money. But the benefit that came up most often was that it had given them confidence in talking to people, especially strangers. A lot of the first-years said they'd been quite shy before."),
            M("Josh", "That's a nice finding. Now, the questionnaire gives us numbers, but not much detail. I was thinking we could interview some employers as well."),
            F("Nadia", "That would take ages to arrange. I think it'd be more useful to do follow-up interviews with a small group of the students, maybe six or eight, to find out more about their experiences."),
